# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Oversite dashboard (frontend) — environment variables
#
# These VITE_* values are compiled INTO the browser bundle at build time, so
# they are public by definition. NEVER put a service-role key or any write-
# capable secret here. Server-side secrets live in Supabase Edge Function
# secrets (listed at the bottom), not in this file.
#
# Local dev:   copy to `.env` and fill in your project's values.
# Railway:     set these as service variables (the Dockerfile passes them in
#              as build args so Vite can bake them into the bundle).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Your Supabase project — Project Settings → API
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR_PROJECT_REF.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=YOUR_ANON_PUBLIC_KEY
VITE_SUPABASE_PROJECT_ID=YOUR_PROJECT_REF

# Payments client/publishable token (safe for the browser). Leave blank if unused.
VITE_PAYMENTS_CLIENT_TOKEN=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOT frontend env — set these in Supabase (Edge Functions → Secrets), never here:
#
#   SUPABASE_URL, SUPABASE_ANON_KEY, SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY
#   STRIPE_LIVE_API_KEY, STRIPE_ENVIRONMENT, INTERNAL_CHARGE_SECRET
#   DISCORD_CLIENT_ID, DISCORD_CLIENT_SECRET, DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN,
#   OVERSITE_UTILITIES_BOT_TOKEN, WORKER_TOKEN
#   RAILWAY_API_TOKEN, RAILWAY_PROJECT_ID, RAILWAY_ENVIRONMENT_ID,
#   RAILWAY_PRODUCTION_ENVIRONMENT_ID
#   ROBLOX_COOKIE, HCAPTCHA_SECRET_KEY, TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY, LEGACY_ANON_JWT
#
# Lovable-specific — MUST be replaced when leaving Lovable:
#   LOVABLE_API_KEY, LOVABLE_SEND_URL
#   The transactional-email functions send through Lovable's API. Off Lovable,
#   point these at your own email provider (Resend / Postmark / SendGrid).
#   See MIGRATION.md → "Email".
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
